    "interpretation": "The gain comes almost entirely from the Neutral class, and it is bought by predicting Neutral far less often. That is the right direction for this corpus: three-star reviews are genuinely rare in delay complaints, and a model that produces four times as many Neutral labels as there are three-star reviews is not undecided, it is wrong in a way that quietly flattens every time series built on it. The rule is a post-hoc threshold, so the Round 2 deliverable is still the model that ships; what changed is how its output is read."
